Package: drcTMB
Title: Fitting Dose-Response Curves Using the Template Model Builder
Version: 0.0.0.9940
Authors@R: 
    person("Daniel", "Gerhard", , "00gerhard@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9336-3454"))
Description: Fits non-linear dose-response models (log-logistic, Weibull,
    log-normal, Gompertz, hormesis, threshold, Michaelis-Menten, and the
    gamma, multistage, exponential and power models of the benchmark dose
    software of the US EPA and of 'PROAST'), optionally with covariates and
    random effects on the parameters, using the Template Model Builder
    ('TMB', Kristensen et al. (2016) <doi:10.18637/jss.v070.i05>) with the
    Laplace approximation for the random effects. The interface follows the
    'drc' package (Ritz et al. (2015) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0146021>).
    The response can be Gaussian, lognormal, binomial, beta-binomial, beta,
    Poisson, negative binomial or time-to-event counts, and Gaussian and
    lognormal residuals can be correlated or heteroscedastic. Estimation is
    by maximum likelihood, or by the posterior mode with priors. Effective
    doses and benchmark doses come with standard errors by automatic
    differentiation and with profile likelihood, bootstrap or robust
    sandwich intervals; benchmark doses can be averaged over models with
    information criteria or by Bayesian model averaging as recommended by
    the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA Scientific Committee (2022)
    <doi:10.2903/j.efsa.2022.7584>).
